                                        "entry_id": "db59f7c9-567a-3207-9d41-e77af23037a6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cause to form a convex curve or surface; to make convex."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1fc4c54e-2380-4d79-86c2-1909437a0c51",
                                                "sense_id": "7819555e-9207-3085-bb8f-5d428f0f008c",
                                                "text": "The back edge of the saw being under the lip of the cleat, use the anvil for a fulcrum and press down on the edge of the saw opposite, which will convex the plate, as the springing up concaved it, and the action of the fast and loose will be the reverse; that is, the fast will go down and the loose come up."
                                            },
